From: "Mira (mira/mira)" <hey2missmira@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 17:42:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] (be) snapshot-remote-unwind variant TU: capture +
 libunwind remote walk
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add `print_stack_snapshot_remote_unwind.cpp`. The variant ships two
hooks the new collector calls into:

  capture_into_slot
    Handler-side body. Saves the interrupted thread's `ucontext_t` into
    `g_snapshots[seq & 1]`, then copies a bounded stack tail starting
    at RSP via `process_vm_readv`. Both operations are signal-safe; the
    syscall copies in the kernel so the user-side walk does not pass
    through ASAN's memcpy interceptor. A `mincore` gate on the first
    page distinguishes "no stack to capture" from "stack present but
    short". `g_slot.status` stays OK and `frame_count` stays 0 — the
    coordinator does not read the slot's PC array for this variant.

  variant_walk_snapshot
    Coordinator-side libunwind remote walk. Builds an `unw_accessors_t`
    with custom `access_reg` / `access_mem` / `find_proc_info` /
    `put_unwind_info`, calls `unw_create_addr_space`, hands the
    snapshot pointer to the accessors via a TLS pointer
    (`tls_active_snapshot`), seeds with `unw_init_remote(&snap->regs)`,
    walks via `unw_step` + `unw_get_reg(UNW_REG_IP)` up to
    `kMaxSignalFrames`, and resolves each PC via
    `detail::pc_to_frame`.

Accessor specifics, all from docs/design/snapshot.md "Decisions":

  - `access_reg`: reads x86_64 GPRs from `snap->regs.uc_mcontext.gregs`.
    Writes return `-UNW_EREADONLYREG`.
  - `access_mem`: serves stack words from `snap->stack_bytes` for
    addresses in `[stack_base, stack_base + stack_size)`. For
    in-stack addresses above the captured tail returns `-UNW_EINVAL`
    (fail closed; libunwind stops and reports the frames so far).
    Other addresses are eh_frame / DSO data — live read with a
    `mincore` guard.
  - `find_proc_info` / `put_unwind_info`: delegate to
    `_Ux86_64_dwarf_find_proc_info` / `_Ux86_64_dwarf_put_unwind_info`.
    Declared with `extern "C"` because the public headers don't
    expose them; `libunwind-x86_64.a` exports them.
  - `get_dyn_info_list_addr`, `access_fpreg`, `resume`,
    `get_proc_name`: not used; return sentinel codes.

The TU does NOT define `UNW_LOCAL_ONLY` before `<libunwind.h>`. The
default `libunwind.a` archive ships `_ULx86_64_init_remote` as a
6-byte stub returning `-UNW_EINVAL` (its body is compiled out under
`UNW_LOCAL_ONLY` in `src/x86_64/Linit_remote.c`), so the remote-mode
API is reachable only via the `_Ux86_64_*` symbols in
`libunwind-x86_64.a`. With the define omitted, libunwind.h's macros
resolve `unw_*` to the `_U` symbols; the link is satisfied by the
companion patch that adds `libunwind-x86_64.a` to thirdparty.

`be/src/service/CMakeLists.txt` globs `*.cpp` recursively; the new TU
is picked up without a CMakeLists edit.

Spec: docs/design/snapshot.md "Scope", "Multi-threaded interactions",
      "Decisions", "Files".

Co-Authored-By: jover <joverzh@gmail.com>
